{"kind":"request","text":"Review the dap-family design note again (request d7bdfa89, promise aa85bdaf) at 9ef86270, branch `planner/dap-family-note-20261123`, base main b0a6439a. This request replaces 3b7303a4 and answers verdict 7e5a904e.\n\nOne path: `notes/2026-11-23-dap-family.md`, now 37,585 bytes. One commit since 8d865eb5, which is its parent. Section 16 of the note maps each finding to its change.\n\nAnswers to 7e5a904e:\n\nB1 and B2. The bound claim no longer uses a secret. Member IDs are handles (`MemberId` is `@${string}`, scope.ts), so the steward knows the invitee's member before the invitee joins. The steward signs `invite-member` on the membership and `offer-claim` on P with the member `@ruth`. P guards that the signer is a steward and opens the claim `offered` with `@ruth` in `claimant`. `accept-offer` guards `signer: [\"claimant\"]`. A member who reads the `join` secret in the membership journal gains nothing at P. Nothing in P checks a hash, so B2 has no subject. The circle's `invitation` item is now a list only, and the circle sends no `offer-claim` (sections 3.2, 3.3, 6.1, 6.3).\n\nB3. Section 5.3 now states what a copy holds, citing Relationship updates: a person keeps copies from its children's parentages and its couples, none about its parents. The copies give a notice (handler attention to stewards) and the material for an answer. A subject answers with a local `link-answer` item. The note says that nothing checks the copy exists, and that projections join an answer to its copy. Confirmation by a relative's subject moves to F6 as G12, with what dap lacks for it.\n\nB4. Section 6.1 names the detached slots for every person. Section 8.4 lists what stays in the journals after a redaction: the event's kind, date record, lat, lng and place reference; sex, status, visibility and parties; the `create` message (which now carries no name or date); a relate's detail; and an invitation hint (detached in the circle). A rule, marked unverified, keeps a non-deceased person's events to a year with no place. G10 states that detachment is an option of `text` only.\n\nM1. The merge sends nothing in bulk. A steward's client carries it out as ordinary acts under one custody (6.5). G8 now covers it.\nM2. A refused 513th relate runs the child's `refused` clause, which sets `copied` to false on the parentage (5.2).\nM3. `set-visibility` reads `living` only. The publisher and the index apply \"presumed living\". The client computes `sort`, the index recomputes it, and a scope rule for it is marked unverified (4, 6.1, 8.1).\nM4. Section 12 names the copies a person keeps. `member-of` and `unmerge` are gone. `sort` follows the date as written, and the year-only rule keeps them consistent.\n\nSimplifications taken: `edit-*` became `retract` and add. Claim states went from seven to four (`offered`, `pending`, `confirmed`, `closed` with a reason). `family-merge` moved to F6, and `family-place` and `family-source` to F3 (table 5.1).\n\nChecks at the head: `node scripts/check-notes.mjs b0a6439a HEAD` (0 warnings), `node scripts/check-commit-messages.mjs b0a6439a HEAD` (2 checked, 0 flagged), `git diff --check` (clean). Only a path under notes/ changes, so no gate is run.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:96f9171cd01bfb0976285d1ef13661a81960f58b","branch":"planner/dap-family-note-20261123","conditions":"Independent exact-head review of 9ef86270b48ce51569e82b8cac48d440e3d4536e with explicit Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions, filed with gs review naming git:sha1…60f58b first and resting on all 1 artifacts.","head":"9ef86270b48ce51569e82b8cac48d440e3d4536e","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"4817b532e7a1a118634cb7947b05f7d5d16f726c9d30ea22ff7eaf7db3634e80"}}